 R←Test_Misc_012(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;proj;parms
⍝ Exercise `CreateRelease`. A stub project is passed so that the test does not depend
⍝ on which Cider projects happen to be open.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 proj←⎕NS''
 proj.CiderConfig←⎕NS''
 proj.CiderConfig.HOME←##.CiderConfig.HOME
 proj.CiderConfig.CIDER←⎕NS''
 proj.CiderConfig.CIDER.project_url←'https://github.com/aplteam/GitHub'
 proj.CiderConfig.CIDER.distributionFolder←'Dist'

 parms←##.GitHub.CreateRelease proj
 →T.PassesIf'aplteam'≡parms.owner
 →T.PassesIf'GitHub'≡parms.repo
 →T.PassesIf 0<≢parms.version
 →T.PassesIf parms.tag≡'v',parms.version
 →T.PassesIf parms.releaseTitle≡'Version ',parms.version   ⍝ As the release page labels it
 →T.PassesIf(⊂parms.prerelease)∊0 1
 →T.PassesIf 1=parms.draft                    ⍝ Nothing must become public by accident
 →T.PassesIf 1=⍴⍴parms.missing
 ⍝ This project is a Tatin package, so its ZIP goes to tatin.dev rather than to GitHub:
 →T.PassesIf 1=parms.tatinPackage
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢parms.assets
 →T.PassesIf'To be consumed as a Tatin package, see https://tatin.dev'≡⊃⌽parms.body
 ⍝ The indentation History carries must be gone, or Markdown sees a code block:
 →T.PassesIf'* '≡2↑⊃parms.body
 ⍝ …and the user commands and flags in it must be marked up as code:
 →T.PassesIf∨/'`]ReportAllIssues`'⍷⊃,/parms.body,¨⊂' '
 →T.PassesIf∨/'`-filename=`'⍷⊃,/parms.body,¨⊂' '
 ⍝ Whatever assets there are must be relative to the project, never absolute:
 →T.PassesIf~∨/{(':'∊2↑⍵)∨'/'=⊃⍵}¨parms.assets

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
